.TH BIGFLOATADD 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatAdd, bigFloatSub, bigFloatMul \- perform signed float arithmetic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigFloatAdd(BigFloat *result, const BigFloat *a, const BigFloat *b);
int bigFloatSub(BigFloat *result, const BigFloat *a, const BigFloat *b);
int bigFloatMul(BigFloat *result, const BigFloat *a, const BigFloat *b);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Computes a plus b, a minus b, or a times b. Output may alias either input.
Every object including the destination must be initialized.
Operations round toward zero at the destination's precision, including aliases.
.PP
Addition retains guard bits and discarded-tail information. Working precision
covers both input widths and output precision to preserve cancellation with
mixed precisions while bounding alignment for distant exponents.
Multiplication forms an exact dynamic integer product before rounding.
Exponent arithmetic is checked before publishing.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0, -1 for allocation/transform failure, INT_MAX for unrepresentable
size/exponent, or -2 for invalid precision. Output is unchanged on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
